# @consola/sandbox: Consola's E2B account, for its live tests and for building templates.
#
# Where: copy this file to packages/sandbox/.env (cp .env.example .env, in this folder).
# Read by:
#   - the package's tests (`pnpm --filter @consola/sandbox test`): with a key, the contract also
#     runs against real E2B sandboxes; without one that run is skipped (the test run says so) and
#     only the fake provider is tested, as in CI. Each live run starts real sandboxes on Consola's
#     account and takes about a minute and a half.
#   - `pnpm --filter @consola/sandbox template:build <name>`, which builds templates/<name>.
#   - `pnpm --filter @consola/host template:build`, which builds the cloud session template
#     (consola-session), when E2B_API_KEY is not already set in the shell.
# Nothing here is a real credential; never commit your .env.
#
# The runner that starts cloud sessions does not read this file: it takes the same key in
# packages/host/.env (packages/host/.env.example).

# Consola's E2B API key (e2b.dev → Dashboard → API Keys).
E2B_API_KEY=
